<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch Oct consumer spending rises 5.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Dutch Oct consumer spending rises 5.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch consumer spending rose 5.1 percent in October 1996 compared to the same month in 1995 and +3.3 percent from January until October, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p> DUTCH CONSUMER SPENDING     Oct 1996  Sept 1996   Jan-Oct 1996</p>
<p>yr-on-yr pct volume changes</p>
<p>(Rises except when otherwise indicated)</p>
<p> Total consumer spending	 5.1	1.0	     3.3</p>
<p>  - food, beverages, tobacco   9.7     -4.9	     3.1</p>
<p>  - durable goods		  8.1	1.1	     4.8</p>
<p>  - other goods and services   3.4	2.3	     3.0</p>
<p>The CBS said the strong increase in food and beverages and durable goods in October 1996 was partly due to a positive calendar effect, as October 1996 included a Sunday and Monday less than the previous year and a Wednesday and Thursday more.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
